Display managers such as lightdm start the session command for Wayland
sessions before the VT switch to the session's VT has completed, so the
logind session is still inactive when cosmic-comp starts. cosmic-comp's
KMS backend silently skips every DRM device while its libseat session is
inactive (device_added returns no outputs) and then aborts with
"Backend initialized without output", leaving a blank screen with a
blinking cursor. KWin tolerates this by waiting for activation;
cosmic-comp does not.

Wait (up to 10s) for logind to report the session Active before
starting cosmic-session. No-op when the session is already active or
when XDG_SESSION_ID/loginctl are unavailable.

--- a/data/start-cosmic	2026-09-29 22:43:37.415803154 +0300
+++ b/data/start-cosmic	2026-09-29 22:43:37.430069349 +0300
@@ -109,6 +109,19 @@
     done
 fi
 
+# Wait for logind to mark this session active before starting the
+# compositor. Display managers such as lightdm launch Wayland sessions
+# before the VT switch completes; cosmic-comp silently skips every DRM
+# device while its libseat session is inactive and then exits with
+# "Backend initialized without output", leaving a blinking cursor.
+if [ -n "${XDG_SESSION_ID}" ] && command -v loginctl >/dev/null; then
+    i=0
+    while [ "$(loginctl show-session "${XDG_SESSION_ID}" -p Active --value 2>/dev/null)" = "no" ] && [ "$i" -lt 100 ]; do
+        sleep 0.1
+        i=$((i + 1))
+    done
+fi
+
 # Run cosmic-session
 if [ -z "${DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS}" ]; then
     exec /usr/bin/dbus-run-session -- /usr/bin/cosmic-session
